# UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer suppressions for the tests of a sanitized build
# (ALAddTestBinary.cmake gives the runs this file). One per line:
#
#   <check>:<function, source file or library>
#
# where <check> is the name a report gives in brackets, such as alignment or
# signed-integer-overflow (report_error_type is on). A suppression is for code
# that is not ours -- a port's headers inlined into ours, a system library --
# and says above it what it hides, why it cannot be fixed here, and where it
# was reported upstream. Our own undefined behaviour is fixed, not listed.
